  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Using standard contracts",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Plan > Strategy and plan",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN outlines three standard contracts that may be used by central government departments, their executive agencies and non-departmental public bodies (collectively referred to as ‘in-scope organisations’). The standard contracts in the suite are:",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "The Model Services Contract (MSC) for complex services procurements which typically require some form of formal dialogue or negotiation with potential suppliers. Use of the MSC is encouraged where the likely contract value (over the whole of the intended contract term) is £20m or more",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "The Mid-Tier Contract for goods and / or services procurements which are not particularly complex and do not require formal dialogue or negotiation with potential suppliers. The Mid-Tier Contract may be used where the likely contract value (over the whole of the intended contract term) is above relevant procurement thresholds, but falls below approximately £20m. It may also be used if a contract is more complex or critical, but below relevant procurement thresholds, and",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "The Short Form Contract for low value goods and / or services procurements where the likely contract value is below the relevant procurement thresholds, unless the contract is more complex or critical, in which case, another contract, such as the Mid-Tier Contract may be used. It should not be used for above-threshold procurements.",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Where in-scope organisations are purchasing bespoke goods or services, or goods or services that cannot be facilitated by a suitable government framework, they should adopt one of the standard contracts above, rather than creating a bespoke contract.",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Where appropriate, standard contracts should be used by in-scope organisations, rather than bespoke contracts being created.",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations should:",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "consider the appropriateness of using a standard contract, rather than creating a bespoke contract. In particular, consideration should be given to the use of standard contracts where bespoke goods or services are purchased which cannot be facilitated by a suitable government framework.",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Legal framework",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN should be read alongside the relevant parts of the legal framework but it is not designed to provide guidance on a particular clause or regulation from the Public Contracts Regulations 2015.",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Additional support and guidance",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Make sure you:",
      "ordinal": 16,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00017",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "read the PPN and any supporting implementation guidance",
      "ordinal": 17,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00018",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "seek legal and commercial advice in the context of specific procurements",
      "ordinal": 18,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00019",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "See also (where relevant and appropriate to do so):",
      "ordinal": 19,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00020",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "The Model Services Contract (MSC)",
      "ordinal": 20,
      "heading_path": [
        "Using standard contracts",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00021",
